#  ######  ######  ######  ######   ####   ######
#    ##    ##        ##    ##  ##    ##    ##
#    ##    ####      ##    ######    ##    ######
#    ##    ##        ##    ## ##     ##        ##
#    ##    ######    ##    ##  ##   ####   ######
#
#  TETRIS written in pure Brainfuck
#
#  Every byte of game logic in this file is one of the eight Brainfuck
#  instructions  Everything else is a comment line that starts with a hash
#  and never contains an instruction character  so you may read it freely
#
#  Requirements for the interpreter
#    eight bit wrapping cells
#    at least 4096 cells of tape
#    end of input either leaves the cell alone or stores zero or 255
#
#  Time
#    Brainfuck has no clock  A tick is an input byte equal to zero
#    (or 255 which some interpreters produce at end of input)
#    Feed ticks by running the terminal with a read timeout
#    or by piping NUL bytes in alongside the keyboard  See the README
#
# ==========================================================================
#  TAPE LAYOUT
# ==========================================================================
#
#  cells 1 to 28     score as seven decimal digit blocks
#                    block i starts at 1 plus 4i  and holds  d c x y
#                    d is the digit  c is a pending carry into it
#                    x and y are private scratch cells
#  cells 29 to 32    phantom block that swallows score overflow
#  cells 33 to 44    lines cleared  three digit blocks  same format
#  cells 45 to 48    phantom block
#  cells 49 to 56    level  two digit blocks
#  cells 57 to 60    phantom block
#  cells 61 to 67    the seven bag  one flag per tetromino still in the bag
#  cell 68   BAGN    tetrominoes left in the bag
#  cell 69   RNG     random state  stirred by every input byte and every tick
#  cell 70   IN      last input byte
#  cell 71   CLR     lines cleared by the last lock
#  cell 72   SOFT    one while the player holds soft drop
#  cell 73   GRAV    ticks left until gravity pulls the piece down
#  cell 74   SPD     ticks per row at the current level
#  cell 75   LV      level as a plain number
#  cell 76   LNC     lines still needed for the next level
#  cell 77   KICK    which wall kick test is being tried
#  cell 78   RDIR    zero for clockwise  one for counterclockwise
#  cell 79   CANHOLD one if hold is allowed for this piece
#  cell 80   HOLD    held piece plus one  or zero when empty
#  cell 81   NEXT    next piece
#  cell 82   GY      row of the ghost piece
#  cell 83   RET     state to return to after a TRY
#  cell 84   RUN     main loop flag
#  cell 85   STATE   current state of the machine
#  cell 86   SW      scratch copy of STATE consumed by the dispatcher
#  cell 87   SF      dispatcher flag  this is HOME for every state
#  cells 88 to 95    T0 to T7 general scratch
#  cell 96   PX      piece column  (of the 4 by 4 box corner)
#  cell 97   PY      piece row
#  cell 98   PT      piece type  0 I  1 O  2 T  3 S  4 Z  5 J  6 L
#  cell 99   PR      piece rotation 0 to 3
#  cell 100  OK      result of the last TRY  one when the spot is free
#  cells 101 to 104  CX CY CT CR  the candidate a TRY will test
#  cells 105 106     U0 U1 copy scratch
#  cell 107  PRIME   one until the first two pieces are dealt
#  cells 108 to 119  scratch for the preview pictures
#  cells 120 to 127  start sentinel  a fake board cell whose F is zero
#  cells 128 on      the board
#
#  THE BOARD
#    30 rows of 16 columns  each square is 8 tape cells wide
#      F  one on every board square  zero on both sentinels
#      B  what is settled there  0 empty  1 to 7 colour  8 wall
#      T  the piece being tested or shown  holds its colour
#      G  ghost marker  holds its colour
#      four scratch cells used to carry values while walking the board
#    rows 0 to 3     ceiling of walls
#    rows 4 and 5    hidden spawn rows
#    rows 6 to 25    the visible ten by twenty well
#    rows 26 to 29   floor of walls
#    columns 0 to 3 and 14 and 15 are walls  columns 4 to 13 are the well
#    after the last square comes the end sentinel whose F is zero
#
#  Since F is one everywhere on the board a loop that steps eight cells
#  at a time while F is nonzero always finds the way back to a sentinel
#  That is how every walk across the board gets home again
#
#  THE MACHINE
#    One loop runs forever  Each pass copies STATE and dispatches it
#    through a nested decrement switch  There are no subroutines in
#    Brainfuck so the shared piece test TRY is a state of its own
#    A caller stores its continuation in RET and jumps to TRY
#
#     0 INIT       title screen and seeding
#     1 DRAW       carry the decimal counters and paint the frame
#     2 INPUT      read one byte and decide
#     3 TRY        draw the candidate on layer T and test it
#     4 LEFT       5 RIGHT      6 MOVE RESULT
#     7 DOWN       8 DOWN RESULT
#     9 ROTATE    10 ROTATE TRY 11 ROTATE RESULT
#    12 HARD DROP 13 LOCK       14 LOCK STAMP
#    15 CLEAR LINES            16 SCORE
#    17 NEXT PIECE 18 SPAWN    19 SPAWN RESULT
#    20 GHOST     21 GHOST TRY  22 GHOST RESULT 23 GHOST STAMP
#    24 HOLD      25 GAME OVER
#
# ==========================================================================

